dHouse requires two services to run: dhouse itself and dhouse.proxy.
The dHouse service is responsible for running scenes, logging activity, and sending notifications.
The dHouse Proxy service acts as an intermediary between the MQTT broker and JavaScript connections.

The dHouse service is built using PHP, while the Proxy service is developed in Python 3.
To run the proxy server, Python 3 must be installed on your Linux system.

Installation
------------

Copy the file dhouse.service from "services" folder to /etc/systemd/system.
	/dhouse.service/ file

	[Unit]
	Description=dHouse remote device control
	After=network.target 

	[Service]
	Type=simple
	User=www-data
	Group=www-data
	ExecStart=/usr/bin/php /usr/local/dhouse/service/dhouse_service.php
	ExecReload=/bin/kill -s SIGUSR1 $MAINPID
	KillMode=process
	Restart=always
	RestartPreventExitStatus=255
	WorkingDirectory=/usr/local/dhouse/service

	[Install]
	WantedBy=multi-user.target

Copy the file dhouse_proxy.service from "proxy" folder to /etc/systemd/system.
	/dhouse_proxy.service/ file

	[Unit]
	Description=dHouse Proxy
	After=network.target 

	[Service]
	Type=simple
	User=root
	Group=root
	ExecStart=/usr/bin/python3 /usr/local/dhouse/proxy/dhouse_proxy.py
	ExecReload=/bin/kill -s SIGUSR1 $MAINPID
	KillMode=process
	Restart=always
	RestartPreventExitStatus=255
	WorkingDirectory=/usr/local/dhouse/proxy

	[Install]
	WantedBy=multi-user.target

-Start services:

> systemctl daemon-reload
> systemctl start dhouse
> systemctl start dhouse_proxy


Both services must be running.
You can test them using next commands:

> systemctl status dhouse

You should get a similar information:

● dhouse.service - dHouse remote device control
     Loaded: loaded (/etc/systemd/system/dhouse.service; enabled; preset: enabled)
     Active: active (running) since Tue 2025-07-22 18:29:00 -03; 1 day 13h ago
   Main PID: 202093 (php)
      Tasks: 1 (limit: 9354)
     Memory: 7.4M
        CPU: 3min 2.370s
     CGroup: /system.slice/dhouse.service
             └─202093 /usr/bin/php /usr/local/dhouse/service/dhouse_service.php

> systemctl status dhouse_proxy

● dhouse_proxy.service - dHouse Proxy
     Loaded: loaded (/etc/systemd/system/dhouse_proxy.service; enabled; preset: enabled)
     Active: active (running) since Wed 2025-07-23 19:25:00 -03; 12h ago
   Main PID: 211069 (python3)
      Tasks: 2 (limit: 9354)
     Memory: 37.0M
        CPU: 51.964s
     CGroup: /system.slice/dhouse_proxy.service
             └─211069 /usr/bin/python3 /usr/local/dhouse/proxy/dhouse_proxy.py


The proxy server is not exposed to the Internet.
The connection is established by Apache, which is also responsible for handling security.
To enable this connection, you need to configure the Apache proxy and tunnel module.

> a2enmod proxy
> a2enmod proxy_http
> a2enmod proxy_wstunnel

Add next lines to your Apache configuration virtual host:
[/etc/apache2/sites-available/000-default.conf]

	<virtualhost [your virtual host]>

     	ProxyPass "/ws/" "ws://localhost:8080/ws/"
      	ProxyPassReverse "/ws/" "ws://localhost:8080/ws/"

Restart Apache

> systemctl restart Apache2
